      "description": "Fetch a legal text, or one of its articles, as it stood on a given date. Returns the version in force at `date` (omit for today): full text, status, validity dates, and the timeline of all versions: say which version you quote. The text carries inline markdown links to cross-referenced articles (/norm/, open with get_norm; when served at a date, the links point to the same date). `commentaires` links out to commentary anchored on the article. `num` absent means you hold the whole text; the `url` of an article's `section`, or of a `section` entry of `articles`, returns all its articles at once.",
